# Frontend and backend are served from the same Railway Express app
# (server.js serves dist/ statically - see "FRONTEND STATIC FILES" in
# server.js). VITE_API_URL is intentionally left unset so src/api.js's
# `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || ""` falls back to same-origin relative
# requests (/api/...), which are correct regardless of what domain Railway
# assigns this service - a hardcoded absolute URL here goes stale the
# moment Railway's public domain changes (exactly what broke login).